      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nLocation ST. LOUIS, MO 63108&#xa;&#xa; Scheduled Hours 40 Position Summary Provides administrative assistance and office support the Obstetrics & Gynecology Department Business office, including the Office of the Chair and Vice Chair of Faculty Development. Job Description Primary Duties & Responsibilities: Administrative Assistant to the Executive Director. Functions as back up to the Assistant to the Chair in times of absence. Works with the Vice Chair of Faculty Development, responsible for the administration of faculty Grand Rounds and Professional Development Series (PDS) as well as the appointments & Promotions process. Anticipates and prepares materials as well as the coordination of various programs, meetings, appointments, etc as well as participates in the facilitation of meetings as required of position. Prepares special reports, summaries, or replies to inquiries, assists with administrative details, often of a confidential nature. May assist with budgetary, operational or related projects, process expenditures, assist with space projects and planning. May provide support related to faculty recruitment. Monitors and assists with guests and daily operations of administrative suite. Other duties as assigned. Working Conditions: Job Location/Working Conditions Normal office environment Physical Effort Typically sitting at a desk or a table Equipment Office equipment The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work performed by people assigned to this classification. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list of all job duties performed by the personnel so classified. Management reserves the right to revise or amend duties at any time. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree Certifications /Professional Licenses : No specific certification/professional license is required for this position. Work Experience: Adm