    "https://wustl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Washington-University-Medical-Campus/Systems-Engineer-I--Hybrid----WashU-IT--Cloud-and-Endpoint-Security_JR96898-1": {
      "title": "Systems Engineer I (Hybrid) - WashU IT, Cloud and Endpoint Security",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nLocation SAINT LOUIS, MO 63110&#xa;&#xa; Scheduled Hours 40 Position Summary Under moderate supervision and technical guidance, responsible for design, implementation, and engineering support for technology solutions with a focus on vulnerability remediation of cloud resources, servers, and workstations. Possess a broad range of technical skills and experience with enterprise-class services. Works with a team of technical staff within the WashU IT organization to ensure that services stay aligned with university initiatives that include research, teaching, patient care, and administrative objectives. Job Description Primary Duties & Responsibilities: Performs research, analyzes technology, consults vendors and applies best practices to design technical solutions by utilizing systems analysis techniques and procedures, including consulting with users, to determine hardware, software or system functional specifications. Typically related to existing system enhancements or new implementations of lesser scale. Validates, tests and implements new products and services. Responds to and resolves incidents escalated from operational teams and performance tuning requests utilizing critical thinking skills. Creates and maintains design documentation related to services, solutions and interfaces. Performs other duties as assigned. Working Conditions: Job Location/Working Conditions Normal Office Environment Physical Effort Typically Sitting at a desk or table Equipment Office Equipment The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work performed by people assigned to this classification. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list of all job duties performed by the personnel so classified. Management reserves the right to revise or amend duties at any time. Required Qualifications Education: Associate degree or combination of education and experience may substitute for minimum education. Certifications /Professional Licenses : No specific certification/professional license is required for this position. Work Experience: Relevant Experience (2 Years) Skills: Not Applicable Driver's License: A driver's license is not required for this position. More About This Job This position will focus on reviewing security alerts in our \"Orca Security\" and \"Tenable\" platforms and coordinating with cloud subscription and system owners to remediate vulnerabilities, risky configurations, and other information security issues. Preferred Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree Certifications /Professional Licenses : Associate Systems Engineering Professional (ASEP) - International Council on Systems Engineering (INCOSE), Certified Systems Engineering Professional (CSEP) - International Council on Systems Engineering (INCOSE), Expert Systems Engineering Professional (ESEP) - International Council on Systems Engineering (INCOSE) Work Experience: No additional work experience unless stated elsewhere in the job posting. Skills: Adaptability, Enterprise Data Warehousing (EDW), Enterprise Operations, Enterprise Technologies, Exercises Judgment, Functional Specifications, High Accuracy, Learning New Technologies, Learning Quickly, Oral Communications, Organizing, Post Secondary Education, Prioritization, Proactive Problem Solving, Professional Education, Self-Starter, SharePoint Integration, SQL Databases, Systems Analysis, Technical Issues, VMware Virtualization, Working Independently, Written Communication Grade G11 Salary Range $53,100.00 - $90,600.00 / Annually The salary range reflects base salaries paid for positions in a given job grade across the University. Individual rates within the range will be determined by factors including one's qualifications and performance, equity with others in the department, market rates for positions within the same grade and department budget. Questions For frequently asked questions 