    "https://wustl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Washington-University-Medical-Campus/Clinical-Research-Study-Assistant-II--Hybrid----Pediatrics-Hematology---Oncology_JR97230": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Study Assistant II (Hybrid) - Pediatrics Hematology & Oncology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nLocation SAINT LOUIS, MO 63110&#xa;&#xa; Scheduled Hours 40 Position Summary Assists investigators with moderately complex clinical research and social science research studies by assisting with enrollments, data, and research compliance needs related to Pediatric Hematology/Oncology and vascular anomalies clinical research. This position will be either fully remote or hybrid in-person and remote work. Position will also participate in qualitative and quantitative data analysis, literature reviews, and grant submissions. Job Description Primary Duties & Responsibilities: Enroll study participants Assist with technical assistance requests.  Assist with data collection, management and analysis.  Conduct literature reviews. Assist with grant and manuscript preparations. Support other study activities as needed. Assist with qualitative and quantitative analysis of datasets. Working Conditions: Job Location/Working Conditions Normal office environment Physical Effort Typically sitting at desk or table Repetitive wrist, hand or finger movement Equipment Office equipment The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work performed by people assigned to this classification. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list of all job duties performed by the personnel so classified. Management reserves the right to revise or amend duties at any time. Required Qualifications Education: High school diploma or equivalent high school certification or combination of education and/or experience. Certifications /Professional Licenses : The list below may include all acceptable certifications, professional licenses and issuers. More than one credential, certification or professional license may be required depending on the role. Basic Life Support - American Heart Association, Basic Life Support - American Red Cross Work Experience: Administrative Or Resear