      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nLocation SAINT LOUIS, MO 63110&#xa;&#xa; Scheduled Hours 40 Position Summary Position performs secretarial duties scheduling patient appointments, completing registration and triaging patient incoming phone calls. Job Description Primary Duties & Responsibilities: Essential Functions : Maintains medical records and notes.    Answers phone, triages call, takes messages and forwards to appropriate persons in EPIC.     Maintains daily appointment schedule for visitors and patient office visits.     Validates and verifies insurance. Facilitates in obtaining prior authorizations for referrals.  Maintains and updates all insurance information for all patients.    Schedules appointments gathering all required information. Receives electronic faxes and roues.   New patient referral process. Sends letters to patients and families.  Other Functions :  Assists administrative /physician staff during peak times, vacations, and illnesses. Greets visitors and routes incoming mail. Facilitates referral to other services at SLCH & outside institutions. Maintains documentation of referrals generated by Late Effects Team screening protocol in Excel. Working Conditions: Job Location/Working Conditions: Normal office environment. Physical Effort: Typically sitting at desk or table. Equipment: Office equipment. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work performed by people assigned to this classification. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list of all job duties performed by the personnel so classified. Management reserves the right to revise or amend duties at any time. Required Qualifications Education: High school diploma or equivalent high school certification or combination of education and/or experience. Certifications /Professional Licenses : No specific certification/professional license is required for this position. Work Experience: M