      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nLocation SAINT LOUIS, MO 63110&#xa;&#xa; Scheduled Hours 40 Position Summary This position is with the Biliary section of Division of Gastroenterology (Department of Medicine) and primarily consists of administrative support services for a Biliary providers including patient calls, maintaining physician's schedule/support and serving as Biliary float, assisting others within the administrative role and providing float coverage. The Biliary section consists of multidisciplinary teams that provide exceptional patient care to these populations. This position performs advanced secretarial duties, such as typing medical dictation, which requires substantial use of medical terminology. This position requires mandatory in-person training and some mandatory in-person meetings. Must be able to come into the office to pick up supplies as needed. Job Description Primary Duties & Responsibilities: Transcribes medical documents such as physician’s letters, correspondence, nurse’s notes and manuscripts; if order entry in the electronic medical record is part of the job function, completes requisitions/orders per WashU guidelines. Maintains physician’s daily appointment schedule and calendar, schedules meetings, arranges conference calls, reserves catering services, makes travel arrangements and completes travel expense reports. Schedules appointments and procedures for patients. Prepares patient charts, including delivering workups. Greets visitors, answers telephone, takes messages and screens patient inquiries, providing information according to departmental procedures and policies. Serves as liaison between patients, physicians and staff, providing routine information to patient inquiries. Assists administrative/clinical staff during peak times, vacations/illnesses. Assists with retrieval and delivery of reports, films, etc. Other duties as assigned. Working Conditions: Normal office environ