    "https://wustl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Washington-University-West-Campus-Clayton-Missouri/Office-Services-Assistant--Advancement-Administration--Time-Limited----University-Advancement_JR96641": {
      "title": "Office Services Assistant, Advancement Administration (Time-Limited) - University Advancement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nLocation SAINT LOUIS, MO 63105&#xa;&#xa; Scheduled Hours 37.5 Position Summary The Office Services Assistant provides entry-level, cross-functional support to the Office Services team across multiple locations. This position assists with reception coverage, mail and delivery services, purchasing support, and basic audio/visual support as needed. The incumbent works under general supervision and will report to the Office Services Manager. The person in this role is expected to demonstrate professionalism, flexibility, and strong customer service in a university environment. Job Description Primary Duties & Responsibilities: Office Support - Provide reception coverage, including greeting visitors, answering telephones, and directing inquiries in a courteous and professional manner.  Receive, sort, process, and distribute incoming and outgoing mail, packages, and interoffice deliveries.  Support daily delivery operations and the distribution of materials across multiple locations.  Assist with purchasing functions, including ordering supplies, tracking requests, and maintaining inventory levels.  Collaborate with team members to ensure continuity of service across supported locations.  Maintain accurate records, logs, and supply areas. Conference Room Management - Serves as a contact for scheduling and managing 26 meeting rooms for University Advancement. This includes providing basic a/v support to select meeting rooms including equipment setup, operation, and troubleshooting. Perform other duties as assigned. Working Conditions: Job Location/Working Conditions Normal office environment Ability to travel to various on- and off-campus locations Physical Effort Typically working at desk or table Repetitive wrist, hand or finger movement Occasional lifting (25 lbs or less) Equipment Office equipment The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work perf