    "https://wustl.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Washington-University-Danforth-Campus/Research-Lab-Technician--Soil-Analysis-Assistant----Earth--Environmental--and-Planetary-Sciences--Part-time-Time-limited-_JR96770": {
      "title": "Research/Lab Technician (Soil Analysis Assistant) - Earth, Environmental, and Planetary Sciences (Part-time/Time-limited)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nLocation ST. LOUIS, MO 63130&#xa;&#xa; Scheduled Hours 30 Position Summary The Catalano Group in Washington University’s Department of Earth, Environmental, and Planetary Sciences is seeking a Research/Laboratory Technician in support of the CLEAN STL Project (https://public-exchange.org/washu/project/clean-stl/partnership/), organized through WashU’s Public Exchange. In collaboration with St. Louis community partners, the assistant will carry out soil sampling and laboratory analyses to evaluate lead exposure risks on residential and commercial properties, process resident-submitted soil samples, and contribute data to project findings reports. This is a time-limited role of up to one year, with the possibility of renewal for a second year contingent on funding. This is a part-time role but there may be opportunities for more hours. Job Description Primary Duties & Responsibilities: Assist in conducting experiments. Assist with miscellaneous projects and experiments. Set up materials/labs. Collect data, maintain files on research, and assist with data entry. Assist with manuscript processing. Order equipment and supplies. Perform other duties as assigned. Working Conditions: Works in a laboratory environment.  Must be physically able to wear protective equipment.  Involves local fieldwork. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work performed by people assigned to this classification. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list of all job duties performed by the personnel so classified. Management reserves the right to revise or amend duties at any time. Required Qualifications Education: High school diploma or equivalent high school certification or combination of education and/or experience. Certifications/Professional Licenses: No specific certification/professional license is required for this position. Work Experience: N