king. Typically bending, crouching, stooping. Ability to lift 50-75 pounds. Ability to travel to various on- and off-campus locations. Equipment Comfort using hand tools and power equipment. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work performed by people assigned to this classification. They are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list of all job duties performed by the personnel so classified. Management reserves the right to revise or amend duties at any time. Required Qualifications Education: High school diploma or equivalent high school certification or combination of education and/or experience. Certifications /Professional Licenses : No specific certification/professional license is required for this position. Work Experience: Maintenance (3 Years) Skills: Not Applicable Driver's License: A Class E (MO) or Class D (IL) license and a good driving record are required for this position. More About This Job Required Qualifications: Relevant vocational degree or certification may substitute for some of the minimum experience required. Preferred Qualifications Education: Vocational Diploma - specific trade or career Certifications /Professional Licenses : No additional certification/professional licenses unless stated elsewhere in the job posting. Work Experience: Trade Functions With Demonstrated Ability To Perform Varied Maintenance Tasks (2 Years) Skills: Cross-Functional Teamwork, Electrical Maintenance, HVAC Solutions, Industrial Maintenance, Interpersonal Communication, Learning Quickly, Oral Communications, Plumbing, Property Assessments, Sound Judgment, Task-Oriented, Teamwork, Working Independently, Written Communication Grade G09-H Salary Range $23.37 - $36.19 / Hourly The salary range reflects base salaries paid for positions in a given job grade across the University. Individual rates within the range will be determined by factors including one's qualifications and performance, equity with others in the d